# REST calls for the demo. Open in VS Code (REST Client extension) or Rider and send one request at a time.
# REST is open in every auth mode; only /mcp is protected.
# Data is reseeded on every start. "tomorrow" = the UTC date after the API started.
# `# expect:` lines are checked by Logistics.Api.Tests/DemoScenes/ArtefactTests.fs (status, then text the body must contain).

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5080

### Health
# expect: 200 Healthy
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### ===== Read path =====

### All Drivers (what get_drivers returns: licences, certificates, Absences, but no Dispatches)
# expect: 200 Lukasz Nowak
GET {{baseUrl}}/drivers

### One Driver
# expect: 200 Lukasz Nowak
GET {{baseUrl}}/drivers/D-01

### Tractor units
# expect: 200 LowDeck
GET {{baseUrl}}/tractors

### Trailers
# expect: 200 Mega
GET {{baseUrl}}/trailers

### Open Transport Orders (ORD-103, ORD-104, ORD-105 tomorrow, more later)
# expect: 200 ORD-103
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders?status=open

### One Transport Order (scene 3: Dangerous goods tomorrow)
# expect: 200 DangerousGoods
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders/ORD-103

### Dispatch options for ORD-103: one option (Lukasz, TRK-02, TRL-02) plus rejection reasons
# expect: 200 D-01
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders/ORD-103/dispatch-options

### Dispatch options for ORD-104 (Mega): no option, both Low deck tractor units are dispatched
# expect: 200 "options":[]
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders/ORD-104/dispatch-options

### Existing Dispatches (seed has DSP-001 to DSP-004). Fallback in scene 4 to show state.
# expect: 200 DSP-001
GET {{baseUrl}}/dispatches

### ===== Dispatch path =====

### Scene 4: dispatch ORD-103 with its only option -> 201, Dispatcher "anonymous" (REST never carries a user)
# expect: 201 "dispatcher":"anonymous"
POST {{baseUrl}}/dispatches
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "orderId": "ORD-103",
  "driverId": "D-01",
  "tractorId": "TRK-02",
  "trailerId": "TRL-02"
}

### Scene 4: Lukasz onto overlapping ORD-105 -> 409, the broken rules as plain text
# expect: 409 Already dispatched on ORD-103
POST {{baseUrl}}/dispatches
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "orderId": "ORD-105",
  "driverId": "D-01",
  "tractorId": "TRK-02",
  "trailerId": "TRL-06"
}

### Dispatches now include DSP-005 for ORD-103
# expect: 200 DSP-005
GET {{baseUrl}}/dispatches

### Cancel DSP-005: ORD-103 is open again
# expect: 204
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/dispatches/DSP-005

### Unknown Dispatch -> 404 with the reason as text
# expect: 404 DSP-005
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/dispatches/DSP-005

### ===== Scene 6 (AppHost profile OAuth) =====

### Scene 6: /mcp without a token -> 401 and WWW-Authenticate: Bearer resource_metadata="…/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/mcp"
# mode: OAuth
# expect: 401
POST {{baseUrl}}/mcp
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream

{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"initialize","params":{"protocolVersion":"2025-06-18","capabilities":{},"clientInfo":{"name":"logistics.http","version":"1"}}}

### Scene 6: Protected Resource Metadata at the URL from WWW-Authenticate -> resource, Keycloak as authorization server, scope
# mode: OAuth
# expect: 200 http://localhost:8080/realms/mcp
GET {{baseUrl}}/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/mcp

### Scene 6: the same metadata at the root path
# mode: OAuth
# expect: 200 mcp:tools
GET {{baseUrl}}/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource
